  "description": "Generate, sign and validate software licenses in .NET. Licenses are signed JSON envelopes (enigma-license/1) whose signature covers the stored payload bytes exactly — there is no canonicalization step to get wrong — and they can be signed with classical RSA (SHA-256/384/512) or post-quantum ML-DSA (FIPS 204, parameter sets 44/65/87). Key pairs are generated, stored and optionally password-encrypted (Argon2id + AES-256-GCM) in a single enigma-key/1 format. A license carries feature flags, arbitrary claims, an optional validity window and an optional device binding; validation is a verdict rather than an exception, reports the first failing check, and supports anchored wildcard product identifiers. All cryptography comes from Enigma.Core.",
