  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First public release. Generates and validates signed software licenses: enigma-license/1 envelopes whose signature covers the stored payload bytes exactly, with no canonicalization step; enigma-key/1 key files covering both algorithm families and both halves of a pair, with optional Argon2id + AES-256-GCM encryption of the private half; and six signature schemes — RSA with SHA-256/384/512 and post-quantum ML-DSA-44/65/87 (FIPS 204). A license carries feature flags, arbitrary claims, an optional validity window and an optional device binding. Validation returns a verdict rather than throwing, reports the first failing check of eight, and supports anchored wildcard product identifiers. Serialization is source-generated, so the library is trim- and AOT-safe. A clean break from Enigma.LicenseManager: its licenses and keys are deliberately not readable here. See RELEASENOTES.md for the full details.",
